[gd_scene load_steps=110 format=3]

; A room, from the inside.
;
; LAYER 4 COULD NOT START WITHOUT THIS FILE. The material library declares
; three scenes and two of them had a .tscn. The interior scene has NINETY-SIX
; materials and 265 rules -- the largest of the three, 40% of the library --
; and not one had ever been rendered, because there was nowhere to render it.
; Layer 3 was declared complete over surfaces nobody had ever seen.
;
; Its material_rules block is written by station/materials.py --export and
; asserted against the library on every run. Everything else here is a
; judgement and is owned by whoever writes it, exactly as in exterior.tscn.
;
; THREE DECISIONS, and each is a difference from the drum scene rather than a
; copy of it:
;
; 1. THERE ARE NO SCENE LIGHTS. Not one. Every source in an interior shot comes
;    from tools/export_scene.py's fixture_lights(), which puts an omni at the
;    centroid of each tagged `light_*` span -- so the light IS the fitting the
;    kit already builds and cannot drift from it. A room with no tagged fitting
;    renders BLACK, and that is the correct answer rather than a bug: a room
;    that lights itself from nowhere is what this arrangement exists to
;    prevent.
;
; 2. AMBIENT IS A TENTH OF THE DRUM'S. The drum is an open volume half a
;    kilometre across with a sun-tube; a corridor is a closed box whose only
;    light is its fittings. NEGATIVE_RESULTS records five separate occasions
;    where a colour in a reference frame turned out to belong to the light, and
;    the corollary is that these rooms are lit hard and locally. Ambient here
;    is a floor that stops unlit geometry being pure black, not a fill.
;
; 3. SSAO RADIUS IS 0.6 m, not 2.5. The drum's subject is a landscape; this
;    one's is a skirting board, a rail band and the reveal above it. At 2.5 m
;    the contact shadow that makes a skirt read as proud of the wall is smeared
;    across the whole wall.

